    "Description": "Red Hat Single Sign-On 7.6 is a standalone server, based on the Keycloak project, that provides authentication and standards-based single sign-on capabilities for web and mobile applications.\n\nThis release of Red Hat Single Sign-On 7.6.13 on RHEL 9 serves as a replacement for Red Hat Single Sign-On 7.6.12, and includes bug fixes and enhancements, which are documented in the Release Notes document linked to in the References.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n* undertow-core: Undertow MadeYouReset HTTP/2 DDoS Vulnerability (CVE-2025-9784)\n* Undertow HTTP Server Fails to Reject Malformed Host Headers Leading to Potential Cache Poisoning and SSRF (CVE-2025-12543)\n* Undertow HTTP Server Fails to Reject Malformed Host Headers Leading to Potential Cache Poisoning and SSRF (CVE-2025-12543)\n* Information disclosure and data deletion via second-order SQL injection (CVE-2026-0603)\n* GOSTCTR implementation unable to process more than 255 blocks correctly (CVE-2025-14813)\n* PKIX draft CompositeVerifier accepts empty signature sequence as valid (CVE-2026-5588)\n* unbounded PGP AEAD chunk size leads to pre-auth resource exhaustion (CVE-2026-3505)\n* High integrity impact due to improper DNS domain name constraint enforcement (CVE-2026-42579)\n* HTTP Request Smuggling due to improper handling of conflicting HTTP/1.0 headers (CVE-2026-42581)\n* HTTP Header Injection via HttpProxyHandler Disabled Validation (CVE-2026-42578)\n* Denial of Service via unbounded memory allocation in HTTP content decompression (CVE-2026-42587)\n* Denial of Service via unbounded memory allocation in HTTP content decompression (CVE-2026-42587)\n* IPv6 subnet rule bypass due to incorrect masking operation (CVE-2026-44249)\n* Denial of Service via malformed HAProxy message (CVE-2026-44893)\n* Denial of Service due to resource leak (CVE-2026-48043)\n* Netty HAProxy PROXY protocol v2 codec: Denial of Service via memory leak from crafted PROXY protocol headers (CVE-2026-48059)\n* Netty has Insufficient Bailiwick Validation for NS Records (CVE-2026-47691)\n* Improper trust manager handling leads to hostname verification bypass (CVE-2026-50010)\n* Information disclosure and data manipulation due to improper CNAME record validation (CVE-2026-45674)\n* Denial of Service due to eager buffer allocation in TLS handshake (CVE-2026-45416)\n* Arbitrary code execution via PolymorphicTypeValidator bypass (CVE-2026-54512)\n* Denial of Service via deeply nested JSON processing (CVE-2026-50193)\n* Denial of Service via incomplete fix in async JSON parser (CVE-2026-68494)\n* Missing authentication on EAP's IIOP NameService leads to MITM or DoS (CVE-2026-15563)\n* Session fixation in OIDC login flow that can lead to account takeover (CVE-2026-7507)\n* Denial of Service via specially crafted SAML input (CVE-2026-7307)\n* Denial of Service due to excessive SAMLRequest decompression (CVE-2026-2575)\n* Denial of Service via excessive processing of OpenID Connect scope parameters (CVE-2026-4634)\n* Unauthorized access via improper validation of encrypted SAML assertions (CVE-2026-2092)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
